st District is one of the closest House races of the cycle. Incumbent Bryan Steil, seeking a fourth term, faces Democrat Mitchell Berman in a district that has been in Republican hands for decades but carries only a slight Republican lean. Recent surveys from late September and early October show the candidates essentially tied, though the most recent public poll is now several weeks old.\n\nSteil holds a substantial fundraising edge and enters with incumbency advantages, while Berman has benefited from significant outside spending against the incumbent. Expert raters are split: five call it Lean Republican, four call it a Tossup, and one rates it a Lean Democratic flip. Prediction markets give Steil roughly a 53-55% chance. The race hinges on whether the favorable Democratic national environment outweighs Steil's structural advantages in the final days.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.3311, "margin": -2.62}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3005, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3258, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3559, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2698, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2844, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2996, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3365, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3287, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3978, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3557, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4029, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3963, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3263, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3374, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3619, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3249, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3362, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.3278, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.3